8.3 close#sensorScopeRefusesAForeignIssue — a check closes only what carries its own label (tools/issues/close.sh)
8.4 run#errorIsNeverTreatedAsClear — a failed check posts nothing and fails the run (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.5 run#hysteresisBothDirections — a close needs N consecutive clear runs (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.6 run#escalatesPastKRecurrences — past K recurrences a check stops reopening (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.7 reopen#refusesANotPlannedClosure — only a completed closure is reopened (tools/issues/reopen.sh)
8.8 sensors#brokenMainFingerprintDistinguishesCauses — the condition fingerprint, not the check id, is the anchor (tools/issues/create.sh)
8.9 sensors#engineNamesNoProjectValue — every row's command comes from the registry (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.10 run#rowsRefusesAnUndeclaredId — a row a step names must be a row the registry declares (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.11 workflow#aRedRecordRunsNoRecordRow — the record rows wait for a build that succeeded (.github/workflows/sensors.yml)
8.12 run#aDelayedTickSelectsTheRowsItWasScheduledFor — the window reaches back over the minutes since the previous tick (tools/sensors/lib.sh)
8.13 workflow#theTickDeclaresItsWindow — every scheduled tick declares the interval it selects over (.github/workflows/sensors.yml)
8.14 run#theWindowDoesNotSelectThePreviousTicksRow — a window that is not a count of minutes is refused (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.15 sensors#aRecordedConditionParsesToItsObject — the recorded condition parses to its object, not to the marker tail (tools/sensors/lib.sh)
8.16 guard#eachCheckHasItsOwnReason — the identity guard reports an unread tracker instead of turning it into a verdict (issue #231) (tools/sensors/guard.sh)
8.17 sensors#sourceSizeRow — a file past the row bound is a violation (tools/sensors/metrics/source-size.sh)
8.18 run#aClearWithNoIssueReachesTheRecord — a clear with no condition issue reaches the tracker on the row's record (issue #257) (tools/sensors/run.sh)
8.19 sensors#metadataDriftRow — a drifted priority pair is a condition, not a clear (issue #292) (tools/sensors/metrics/metadata-invariant.sh)
8.20 report#aFiledRowIsReported — the filing marker in the issue body is part of the row history (issue #668) (tools/sensors/lib.sh)
8.21 run#aFilingSetsTheBaseline — the baseline is the newest marker the row carries, a filing included (issue #668) (tools/sensors/run.sh)
